s chosen to maintain anonymity by not disclosing their gender. To represent themselves in public announcements related to the series, the author uses an avatar of an…</span>\n                </a>\n            \n        </div>\n        \n\n        <div class=\"topic-content\">\n            \n                <div class=\"fact-card\">\n                    <div class=\"fact-label\">\n                        Created By\n                    </div>\n\n                    <h3>\n        <a href=\"/demon-slayer/koyoharu-gotouge\" class=\"entity-link\">\n            Koyoharu Gotouge\n        </a>\n    </h3>\n\n                    <p>Koyoharu Gotouge created Demon Slayer.</p>\n\n                    \n\n                    \n                </div>\n            \n        </div>\n    </details>\n</section>\n\n</section>\n\n\n<section class=\"did-you-know\">\n    <h2>Did you know?</h2>\n    <ul>\n        <li>Demon Slayer is also referenced as Kimetsu no Yaiba, Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba, 鬼滅の刃.</li><li>Koyoharu Gotouge created Demon Slayer.</li><li>The manga is the foundation of Demon Slayer.</li><li>Demon Slayer Manga is a medium branch of Demon Slayer.</li><li>Demon Slayer Anime is a medium branch of Demon Slayer.</li><li>Evidence around Demon Slayer is classified as fiction on Ton-o-Lore.</li>\n    </ul>\n</section>","overview":"<section class=\"overview\">\n    <h2>What is Demon Slayer?</h2>\n    \n    <p>\n        In order to become a Demon Slayer, an individual must pass Final Selection, a test used as an entrance exam to join the Demon Slayer Corps. During this selection, examinees must survive for seven days on the mountain top of Mount Fujikasane, a perilous domain infested with demons. The examinees must rely solely on the skills they have developed in training. The majority of candidates participating in the Final Selection have undergone extensive training under the guidance of a cultivator of a Breathing Style. Only when these candidates have reached a satisfactory level of skill and competence, are they entrusted by their Cultivator to partake in the selection. However, there is one exceptional case of a Demon Slayer who entered on their own volition without previous training.\n    </p>\n    <p>\n        Candidates who complete the Final Selection are issued the standard uniform, as well as being given the opportunity to choose the ore for their Nichirin Sword, which is designed to eliminate demons efficiently. Each new Demon Slayer is also assigned a rare species of talking bird known as the Kasugai Crows for communication purposes.\n    </p>\n    <p>\n        Mizunoto are roughly paid around 20,000 yen whereas Hashira are paid as much as they want.\n    </p>\n    <p>\n        Members of the Demon Slayer Corps are separated into ten different ranks. From lowest rank to highest, these ranks are:\n    </p>\n    \n    <p class=\"also-known-as\">\n        <strong>Also known as:</strong>\n        Kimetsu no Yaiba, Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba, 鬼滅の刃.\n    </p>\n\n</section>","word_count":936,"uniqueness_score":"1.0000"},"entity":{"id":"7d72a0dc-3305-4d60-8c03-a3a925447372","name":"Demon Slayer","slug":"demon-slayer","type":"topic","kind":"topic","type_label":"Topic","short_description":"In order to become a Demon Slayer, an individual must pass Final Selection, a test used as an entrance exam to join the Demon Slayer Corps. During this selection, examinees must survive for seven days on the mountain…","description":"In order to become a Demon Slayer, an individual must pass Final Selection, a test used as an entrance exam to join the Demon Slayer Corps. During this selection, examinees must survive for seven days on the mountain top of Mount Fujikasane, a perilous domain infested with demons. The examinees must rely solely on the skills they have developed in training. The majority of candidates participating in the Final Selection have undergone extensive training under the guidance of a cultivator of a Breathing Style. Only when these candidates have reached a satisfactory level of skill and competence, are they entrusted by their Cultivator to partake in the selection. However, there is one exceptional case of a Demon Slayer who entered on their own volition without previous training.\n\nCandidates who complete the Final Selection are issued the standard uniform, as well as being given the opportunity to choose the ore for their Nichirin Sword, which is designed to eliminate demons efficiently. Each new Demon Slayer is also assigned a rare species of talking bird known as the Kasugai Crows for communication purposes.\n\nMizunoto are roughly paid around 20,000 yen whereas Hashira are paid as much as they want.\n\nMembers of the Demon Slayer Corps are separated into ten different ranks. From lowest rank to highest, these ranks are:","evidence":"fiction","universe":"demon-slayer","aliases":["Kimetsu no Yaiba","Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba","鬼滅の刃"],"wikipedia_url":null,"image_url":null,"image_source":null,"image_credit":null,"image_license":null,"image_usage":null,"image_alt":null},"connections":[],"rabbit_holes":[],"copyright":{"theme":"demon-slayer","title":"Demon Slayer is not owned by Ton-o-Lore.","body":"Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba, its characters, artwork, logos, and related intellectual property are the property of their respective rights holders, including Koyoharu Gotouge, Shueisha, Aniplex, ufotable, and other credited rights holders. Ton-o-Lore is an independent, unofficial fan and informational project and is not affiliated with or endorsed by those rights holders. Identification logos and thumbnails, when shown, are low-resolution images used under a fair-use rationale for commentary and identification only — not free or redistributable artwork."},"subject":{"id":"demon-slayer","name":"Demon Slayer","theme":"demon-slayer","path":"/demon-slayer","logo":{"license":"fair_use","usage":"fair_use_identification","url":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/kimetsu-no-yaiba/images/8/